{
  "text": " Tonight renowned NHS trained cardiologist Dr. Asim Malhotra. He was shortlisted in the Sunday Times as one of the most influential individuals in the UK in the fields of science and medicine, a list which also included Professor Stephen Hawking. You guys are going to be speaking live and that was just a couple of weeks. We are. You know, we've been communicating back and forth for nearly two years now. Prominent, younger, more handsome UK cardiologist. His father takes the vaccine, a very former prominent physician, almost certainly has a vaccine related. Atherosclerotic cardiovascular event dies. Malhotra, who is promoting the vaccines on Good Morning Britain, has to come to the realization that listen, they have big safety issues. I'm somebody that has been a very strong advocate for vaccines. I went to Good Morning Britain several months ago because film director, who's a friend of mine, had vaccine hesitancy and I thought that she was high risk. She discussed it with me. I told her she should have the vaccine. She tweeted it out. They wanted me to come on and explain why vaccine hesitancy was there and how I felt for her it was the right thing to do. He says, I have to do my own analysis. I have to write my own papers and he does it and he gets them published and that's very hard to do. I get them great credit and then he comes out and says I have to warn people. Double jammed and being one of the first to take the Pfizer vaccine. I have after several months, critically appraising the data, speaking to eminent scientists in Oxford, Stanford and Harvard that this vaccine is not completely safe and has unprecedented harms, which leads me to conclude that it needs to be suspended until all the raw data has been released for independent analysis. These researchers at the moment have decided they're not going to publish their findings because they are concerned about losing research money from the drug industry. They're going to be in the Dallas Arboretum. There are folks who want to get in there. Definitely www.vaxsafety.org slash events. Really a brilliant event. You're looking at two of the biggest voices in heart health in the world now standing together, discussing COVID. You're leading us into I think a better world.",
